SQL Queries for Automation Performance & Workforce Efficiency Dashboard

This repository contains the SQL queries used to build the Automation Performance & Workforce Efficiency Dashboard, which integrates data from multiple Teradata sources to analyze store-level automation, workforce productivity, and service quality. The queries are optimized for use in Teradata SQL Assistant or similar SQL execution environments.

Overview

The dashboard provides insights into how automation impacts operational performance, customer experience, and workforce efficiency across pharmacy stores.
It analyzes metrics such as automation utilization, script fill rates, call handling efficiency, abandonment rates, and workforce demand vs. actual hours.

Data is sourced from various Teradata environments including:
	•	RXCOE_SA
	•	RXCOE_EWS
	•	IDW_RX_OPERATIONS_S_BC
	•	IDW_COMMON
	•	RXCOE_WFM

Each query contributes to key performance indicators (KPIs) visualized in the dashboard, supporting trend analysis, operational monitoring, and regional comparisons.

