Core Tables and Queries

1. PK_Automation_Colleague_NPS

Retrieves colleague-level Net Promoter Score (NPS) survey results for automation-related feedback.

SEL * 
FROM rxcoe_sa.PK_Automation_Colleague_NPS;

Purpose:
Provides baseline satisfaction metrics to assess the impact of automation on colleague experience and store performance.

⸻

2. WeCare_Call_Metrics

Calculates call handling KPIs such as abandonment rate, average hold time, and average time to answer, aggregated by store and fiscal week.

Key Fields:

Division, Region, District, Store, Fiscal Week, 
Abandonment_Numerator, Abandonment_Denominator,
AVG_TIME_TO_ANSWER_IN_SECONDS_NUM, AVG_HOLD_TIME_IN_SECONDS_DEN

Purpose:
Measures operational efficiency and customer service performance at the store level.
Supports correlation between automation levels and customer experience metrics.

⸻

3. Automation_Script_Utilization

Calculates total automation scripts, total store scripts, and utilization rate across different robot types (SP100, SP200, KL, CRS, Parata).

Key Dimensions:

Date, Store, Division, District, Region, State, Robot Type, Number of Cells

Key Metrics:
	•	Total Scripts
	•	Total Automation Scripts
	•	Automation Type Indicator (Y/N)

Purpose:
Quantifies automation adoption and efficiency across stores.
Identifies performance trends by automation model type and store configuration.

⸻

4. AVD_Workforce_Hours

Captures pharmacist and technician demand versus actual hours worked (AvD data).

SEL 
fiscal_week_nbr AS "Fiscal Week",
dim_store AS Store,
rph_hrs_demand_adj AS "Rph Demand Hrs",
rph_hrs_act_adj AS "Rph Actual Hrs",
tech_hrs_demand_adj AS "Tech Demand Hrs",
tech_hrs_act_adj AS "Tech Actual Hrs"
FROM RXCOE_WFM.AVD_RX_FS;

Purpose:
Evaluates workforce alignment and staffing efficiency relative to operational demand.
Helps identify potential understaffing or overstaffing issues across regions.

⸻

5. PK_Automation_mTC_Score

Retrieves mTC (mean Time to Complete) automation performance metrics from rxcoe_sa.PK_Automation_mTC_Score.

Purpose:
Tracks average processing time for automated scripts and supports time efficiency analysis.

⸻

6. PK_Automation_Sev1_Data

Retrieves data related to Severity 1 incidents in automation systems from rxcoe_sa.PK_Automation_Sev1_Data.

Purpose:
Used for monitoring critical automation errors or downtime events impacting production efficiency.

